      "hints": [
        "Place $O$ at the origin: $B$ is $4\\mathbf{i}$, $A$ is $-4\\mathbf{i}$ and $C$ is $4\\mathbf{j}$.",
        "Find the position vectors of $P$, $N$ and midpoint $M$; then form vectors from $P$.",
        "Use the dot product and magnitudes to obtain the angle at $P$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$P=(-4,0,12)$, $N=(4,0,4)$ and $M=(0,4,6)$. Therefore $\\overrightarrow{PN}=(8,0,-8)$ and $\\overrightarrow{PM}=(4,4,-6)$.",
        "$\\overrightarrow{PN}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{PM}=8(4)+0(4)+(-8)(-6)=80$. Also $|PN|=\\sqrt{128}$ and $|PM|=\\sqrt{68}$.",
        "$\\cos\\angle MPN=\\frac{80}{\\sqrt{128}\\sqrt{68}}=\\frac5{\\sqrt{34}}$, so $\\angle MPN=31.0^\\circ$ (3 s.f.)."
      ]
    }
  ]
